[{"id":"fm-core1-1.02-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Bruce is attempting to find the solutions to an equation. His attempt is shown below.</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}z^2-2z+5&amp;=0\\\\(z-2)^2-4&amp;=-5\\\\z-2&amp;=\\sqrt{-9}\\\\z&amp;=2\\pm9i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Identify all his mistakes.</p></li><li><p>Write a correct solution.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>On line 2: He doesn't halve the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> inside the bracket when completing the square.</p>","<p>On line 3: He subtracted 4 from the RHS rather than adding it and doesn't put a <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pm\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in front of the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{-9}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On line 4: He didn't square root the 9</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}z^2-2z+5&amp;=0\\\\(z-1)^2-1&amp;=-5\\\\z-1&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-4}\\\\z&amp;=1\\pm2i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.02-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Without using a calculator, find the solutions to each of the following equations. You must show your working:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z^2+1=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z^2+10=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z^2-2z+17=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4z^2-4z+17=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2z^2-2z+1=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z^2-z+3=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}z^2&amp;=-1\\\\z&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-1}\\\\z&amp;=\\pm i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}z^2&amp;=-10\\\\z&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-10}\\\\z&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{10}i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}(z-1)^2-1&amp;=-17\\\\(z-1)^2&amp;=-16\\\\z-1&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-16}\\\\z&amp;=1\\pm4i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}4\\left(z-\\frac12\\right)^2-1&amp;=-17\\\\4\\left(z-\\frac12\\right)^2&amp;=-16\\\\\\left(z-\\frac12\\right)^2&amp;=-4\\\\z-\\frac12&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-4}\\\\z&amp;=\\frac12\\pm2i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}2\\left(z-\\frac12\\right)^2-\\frac12&amp;=-1\\\\2\\left(z-\\frac12\\right)^2&amp;=-\\frac12\\\\\\left(z-\\frac12\\right)^2&amp;=-\\frac14\\\\z-\\frac12&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-\\frac14}\\\\z&amp;=\\frac12\\pm\\frac12i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}\\left(z-\\frac12\\right)^2-\\frac14&amp;=-3\\\\\\left(z-\\frac12\\right)^2&amp;=-\\frac{11}4\\\\z-\\frac12&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-\\frac{11}4}\\\\z&amp;=\\frac12\\pm\\frac12\\sqrt{11}i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.02-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>Find the solutions to each of the following, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a+bi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(z+5)^2=-7\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(z-1)^2=-12\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2(z+4)^2+8=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8(z+5)^2-3=-9\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}(z+5)^2&amp;=-7\\\\z+5&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-7}\\\\z&amp;=-5\\pm\\sqrt7i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}(z-1)^2&amp;=-12\\\\z-1&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-12}\\\\z&amp;=1\\pm\\sqrt{12}i\\\\z&amp;=1\\pm2\\sqrt3i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}2(z+4)^2+8&amp;=6\\\\2(z+4)^2&amp;=-2\\\\(z+4)^2&amp;=-1\\\\z+4&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-1}\\\\z&amp;=-4\\pm i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}8(z+5)^2-3&amp;=-9\\\\8(z+5)^2&amp;=-6\\\\(z+5)^2&amp;=-\\frac34\\\\z+5&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-\\frac34}\\\\z&amp;=-5\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt3}2i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.02-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Without using a calculator, find all the solutions to</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^4+2z^2-3=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>You must show your working.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}z^4+2z^2-3&amp;=0\\\\(z^2+1)^2-1&amp;=3\\\\(z^2+1)^2&amp;=4\\\\z^2+1&amp;=\\pm2\\\\z^2&amp;=1\\text{ or }z^2=-3\\\\z&amp;=\\pm1\\text{ or }z=\\sqrt{-3}=\\pm\\sqrt3i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.02-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>Find the quadratic equation in the form</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^2+bz+c=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>which has roots:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1-i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3+i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3-i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1-2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4+3i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4-3i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-5i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1+\\sqrt2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1-\\sqrt2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;z^2-(1+i+1-i)z+(1+i)(1-i)\\\\&amp;=z^2-z+iz-z-iz+1+i-i+1\\\\&amp;=z^2-2z\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;z^2-(3-i+3+i)z+(3+i)(3-i)\\\\&amp;=z^2-3z+3iz-3z-3iz+9+3i-3i+1=z^2-6z+10\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;z^2-(1+2i+1-2i)z+(1+2i)(1-2i)\\\\&amp;=z^2-z+2iz-z-2iz+1+2i-2i+4=z^2-2z+5\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;z^2-(-4+3i-4-3i)z+(-4+3i)(-4-3i)\\\\&amp;=z^2+4z-3iz+4z+3iz+16+12i-12i+9=z^2+8z+25\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;z^2-(i-i)z+(i)(-i)\\\\&amp;=z^2-iz+iz+1=z^2+1\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;z^2-(5i-5i)z+(5i)(-5i)\\\\&amp;=z^2-5iz+5iz+25=z^2+25\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">g)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;z^2-(-1+\\sqrt2i-1-\\sqrt2i)z+(-1+\\sqrt2i)(-1-\\sqrt2i)\\\\&amp;=z^2+z-\\sqrt2iz+z+\\sqrt2iz+1-\\sqrt2i+\\sqrt2i+2=z^2+2z+3\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.02-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>One root the quadratic equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^2+pz+q=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3-8i\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are real values.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Write down the other root of the equation.</p></li><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3+8i\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}(z-(3+8i))(z-(3-8i))&amp;=z^2-(3+8i)z-(3-8i)z+(3+8i)(3-8i)\\\\&amp;=z^2-3z-8iz-3z+8iz+9+24i-24i+64=z^2-6z+73\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=-6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=73\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.02-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>One root the quadratic equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^2+pz+q=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac12-4i\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are real values.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Write down the other root of the equation.</p></li><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-\\frac12+4i\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{gathered}\\left(z-\\left(-\\frac12-4i\\right)\\right)\\left(z-\\left(-\\frac12+4i\\right)\\right)\\\\\\begin{aligned}&amp;=z^2-\\left(-\\frac12-4i\\right)z-\\left(-\\frac12+4i\\right)z+\\left(-\\frac12-4i\\right)\\left(-\\frac12+4i\\right)\\\\&amp;=z^2+\\frac12z+4iz+\\frac12z-4iz+\\frac14-2i+2i+16\\\\&amp;=z^2+z+\\frac{65}4\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=\\frac{65}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.02-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>One root the quadratic equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^2+pz+q=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a+bi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are real values.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Write down the other root of the equation.</p></li><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a-bi\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}(z-(a+bi))(z-(a-bi))&amp;=z^2-(a+bi)z-(a-bi)z+(a+bi)(a-bi)\\\\&amp;=z^2-az-biz-az+biz+a^2+abi-abi+b^2=z^2-2az+a^2+b^2\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=-2a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=a^2+b^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.02-q9","number":9,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q9: Complex Loci</strong></p><p>The function f is defined as</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=z^2-4z+7\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the roots of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p>The two of the roots of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lie on the locus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C=\\{z:|z|=p\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the area of the region in the Argand diagram enclosed by the locus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p>Another point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies on the locus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Real(w)=-\\Real(z_1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li><p>State the possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p>The function g is defined as</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{g}(w)=w^2+aw+b\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are real constants.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"5\"><li><p>Using your answers to part d) as the roots of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{g}(w)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}z^2-4z+7&amp;=0\\\\(z-2)^2-4&amp;=-7\\\\z-2&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-3}\\\\z&amp;=2\\pm\\sqrt3i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"|2+\\sqrt3i|=\\sqrt{4+3}=\\sqrt7\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=\\sqrt7\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Area is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"w=-2+\\sqrt3i\\text{ or }w=-2-\\sqrt3i\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}(w-(-2+\\sqrt3i))(w-(-2-\\sqrt3i))&amp;=w^2+4w+(-2+\\sqrt3i)(-2-\\sqrt3i)\\\\&amp;=w^2+4w+7\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=7\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.02-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>The equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^2+kz+4=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a real number, has complex roots. Find the range of possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>Distinct complex roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2-4ac&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}k^2-4\\times4&amp;&lt;0\\\\(k-4)(k+4)&amp;&lt;0\\\\\\therefore-4&amp;&lt;k&lt;4\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.02-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>It is given that a quadratic polynomial has non-zero real coefficients, and the linear term is zero. Show that it has purely imaginary roots.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}az^2+c&amp;=0\\\\z^2&amp;=-\\frac ca\\\\z&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{-\\frac ca}\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> it only has purely imaginary roots</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.02-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>It is given that a quadratic polynomial has non-zero real coefficients, and the constant term is zero. Show that it can only have real roots.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}az^2+bz&amp;=0\\\\z(az+b)&amp;=0\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The roots are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=-\\frac ba\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which are real</p>"]}]